pkg:Evidence_v1_20_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.20.0 (STORY-7 closed -- real content-quality fixes)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: user's direct finding -- 'the page is shameful' -- exposed a real gap in this session's own verification discipline: 0 console errors had been repeatedly treated as sufficient evidence of correctness. Took real screenshots for the first time and found genuine, glaring, user-visible defects: the visible header still named the source template's own subject; 'undefined' rendered literally for absent fields; a relation-type table showing all zeros against a real '7 relations' stat directly above it; a footer carrying the source template's own dev debug commentary; a coverage paragraph describing the wrong subject's file-processing history; the source subject's real company name hardcoded into two chat system prompts (the most dangerous finding); three more 'LCW policy' label references. Fixed all of these and re-verified via real Playwright after each fix: 0 errors maintained, confirmed via fresh screenshots. Disclosed honestly rather than silently narrowed: ~39/10 references remain in deep RAG/retrieval logic and test fixtures tied to the source subject's own P01-P20 ID scheme -- not blind-replaced given real breakage risk without dedicated testing; filed as STORY-8, genuinely Proposed, not started. STORY-7 closed with real Evidence scoped precisely to what was actually fixed. Re-verified against the concurrently-updated BRSF (tbox v1.64.0, shacl v1.74.0): pipeline order (37 subjects, reproduces), full SHACL 0 violations."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "2caa8ed882cd8de39fdf11e1ae060c94059a7c12f25eb3ce92107f952b62e5a4"^^xsd:string .
